Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 17:05:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 095/105] N1 stage A integration: SGLANG_MTP_LMHEAD_NVFP4=1

Packs the draft's hot-vocab lm_head as NVFP4 at load time and serves it through
w4a16_nvfp4_gemv. Off by default.

The rows are re-read from the checkpoint shard rather than taken from the FP8 head the
eagle worker has just sliced: by that point the target's weight is already FP8 in place,
and quantising FP8 -> NVFP4 compounds two lossy steps and costs argmax agreement.
safetensors slices lazily, so only the 49152 hot rows are materialised (0.93s) and there
is no 1.27GB transient. Packing is deterministic, so the result is cached next to the
token map under a key over shard identity + tensor name + exact row set; cold start
costs 2.2s, warm 0.14s, and the cached file is 70.8MB against the FP8 slice's 125.8MB.
Verified: the packed weight is bit-identical (0/125829120 values differ) to an
independently packed reference.

NVFP4DenseLinearMethod implements just what logits_processor._compute_lm_head needs
(apply / apply_into into the shared fp32 buffer), with a chunked dequant+GEMM fallback
for the wide-M extend path the M<=16 GEMV cannot serve.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
